messages -> retirement: "Repair9: outcome and cached action are last users; ACK is not complete captured-graph retirement"
execution -> control: "Repair9: query deduplicates within shot, never user multi-shot invocation; closed/materialized/pending alpha populations remain separate"
roots -> retirement: "Repair9: actual RC/full-GC/wait DEV bridge validates controlled query/ACK and reader exclusion; production S/queue authority and native whole-gate evidence stay OPEN"
roots -> execution: "Repair9: actual wait continuation survives original owner exit and two GC-separated user shots; real reflective slot replacement and old alias semantics remain mandatory, not immutable-S admission"
roots -> control: "Repair9: real wait serde preserves native refusal or explicit same-VM identity, captured exception/winding and post-ACK root custody; shared-token alias counterexample stays retained"
control -> retirement: "Repair9: close resolver admission while accepted requests/results retain rooted code/resource scope; ACK ends payload query rights, not physical module lifetime"
control -> roots: "Repair9: pre-registration general fallback differs from post-registration same-wait recovery; query never re-registers and ACK never revokes cached/escaped root users"
collector -> control: "Repair9: selected historical GC repairs do not replace same-wait/service/exit ownership or original-load net-benefit acceptance"
control -> execution: "Repair9: normal wait return without early escape, selected terminal outcome or authorized same-wait rearm, then natural completion and independently drained root users"
roots -> retirement: "Repair9: install protected target before source ACK; real source close and join permit byte-only drain, not arbitrary cross-VM pointer export or final cached-user release"
